# Installer engine boundaries

## Layers

1. **Execution**: `frzr-bootstrap` / `frzr-deploy` noninteractive only (`FRZR_NONINTERACTIVE=1`).
2. **InstallEngine** (`installer/engine/`): `InstallPlan`, argv/env builders, runners, progress events. **No** `gi` / Gtk / Textual / dialog imports.
3. **UI adapters** (GTK `ui/`, future Textual `tui/`): read/write `InstallPlan`, subscribe to `ProgressEvent`. Do not assemble `FRZR_*` or `Popen(frzr-*)` in pages.

## Do / Don't

```python
# ✅ GOOD — page uses engine
plan = InstallPlan.from_app_state(self.app)
BootstrapService(on_event=...).run(plan, log_file=...)

# ❌ BAD — page owns frzr contract
env["FRZR_NONINTERACTIVE"] = "1"
subprocess.Popen(["frzr-bootstrap", ...], env=env)
```

```bash
# ❌ BAD — grow business logic in installer-text.sh
# ✅ GOOD — shell launches Python TUI/engine; hot-update is optional shim only
```

## Local verify (no ISO)

```bash
PYTHONPATH=skorionos/airootfs/usr/local/lib \
  INSTALLER_FRZR_BOOTSTRAP=scripts/installer-stubs/frzr-bootstrap \
  ./scripts/dev-run-engine-bootstrap.sh dual nvme0n1 shrink /dev/nvme0n1p3 60

pytest tests/installer -q
```

Never run real frzr against a host disk from agent sessions unless the user explicitly requests it and sets `INSTALLER_ALLOW_REAL_FRZR=1`.
